\contentsline {table}{\numberline {C.1}{\ignorespaces NL-to-SQL: paired bootstrap tests over test cases (10,000 draws, fixed seed). Per case, correctness is averaged over the seeds both models have; the statistic is the mean over cells of A $-$ B with equal cell weights. Per-seed differences show seed variation, which the case bootstrap does not cover.}}{99}{table.C.1}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {C.2}{\ignorespaces NL-to-Scala: paired bootstrap tests over test cases (10,000 draws, fixed seed). Per case, correctness is averaged over the seeds both models have; the statistic is the mean over cells of A $-$ B with equal cell weights. Per-seed differences show seed variation, which the case bootstrap does not cover.}}{100}{table.C.2}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {C.3}{\ignorespaces NL-to-R: paired bootstrap tests over test cases (10,000 draws, fixed seed). Per case, correctness is averaged over the seeds both models have; the statistic is the mean over cells of A $-$ B with equal cell weights. Per-seed differences show seed variation, which the case bootstrap does not cover.}}{101}{table.C.3}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {C.4}{\ignorespaces Error detection: paired bootstrap tests over test columns (10,000 draws, resampled within each test set, the same draw for both models and all seeds); F1 is recomputed on each draw, averaged over seeds, and the statistic is the mean over ST and RT of A $-$ B.}}{102}{table.C.4}%
